00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.000
 So the thing we're talking about now

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.840
 is we're talking about the JSON 1.py example from the book.

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:43.720
 And so JSON is kind of like XML except a lot simpler.

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:45.680
 And that's why a lot of people like it.

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:47.560
 It's not that JSON is always better,

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:50.640
 but JSON is better in a lot of situations

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:53.080
 that don't require the complexity of XML.

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:55.320
 So we start to import JSON.

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:58.660
 JSON is built into Python, but we have to ask to import it.

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:00.980
 Again, we're using a triple-quoted string

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:03.860
 to put the JSON in there.

00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:06.760
 And JSON looks a lot like Python dictionaries,

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:08.920
 key value pairs, key value pairs.

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:11.960
 In this case, this is a key and the value itself

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:16.680
 is another dictionary or in JSON terms, an object.

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:18.800
 But again, key value pairs within key value pairs

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:20.120
 within key value pairs.

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:22.060
 And all these little cursor guys have to,

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:26.480
 all these little curly brace guys have to line up properly.

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:29.980
 And so, like all the time, this is a string

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:33.980
 which we normally would read and decode from the internet,

00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:36.100
 but for now we're just going to have it in there.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:38.920
 Load JSON.loadS says go into the JSON library,

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:41.420
 pull out load string, and parse this,

00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:46.300
 which turns this set of curly braces, spaces, commas,

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:49.560
 perhaps syntax errors into a structured object.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:52.160
 And if we had made a syntax error in here,

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:53.540
 then this would blow up.

00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:55.520
 But if this doesn't make a syntax error,

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:56.360
 if this doesn't blow up,

00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:59.480
 then we have a structured representation.

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:03.300
 Now the difference between XML and Python, JSON,

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:06.720
 is that this turns into a Python dictionary

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:08.720
 with key value pairs.

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:12.280
 And so once we have this, this is a dictionary.

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:14.640
 And we can say info sub name,

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:17.040
 and that's the exact syntax that we would use

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:17.880
 to get the dictionary.

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:20.920
 And that's going to extract this value out of there.

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:25.600
 And if we want to go in deeper, we can say info sub email,

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:28.520
 and that's what info sub email is right there.

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:29.960
 And then sub hide.

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:32.800
 So that's like, that's a dictionary within a dictionary.

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:36.640
 And so if we run this, Python 3 JSON 1.py,

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:42.800
 it digs in really fast.

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:45.080
 And so this is why people tend to like JSON,

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:47.280
 is because you'll read the JSON,

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:49.640
 which is actually a syntax derived from JavaScript,

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:53.160
 but it looks just like the syntax for a Python.

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:57.160
 So that's moving an object, a JSON object,

00:02:57.160 --> 00:03:00.480
 that turns in directly into a Python dictionary

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:01.760
 with nested dictionaries.

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:03.800
 Now we're going to look at JSON 2.

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:07.320
 And so JSON 2, we're going to see a list,

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:09.280
 or an array in JSON terms,

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:11.600
 but it turns into a list in Python terms.

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:15.400
 So this is a list of dictionaries.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:18.320
 In JavaScript, that would be an array of objects,

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:20.400
 but in Python, it's a list of dictionaries.

